| | Humans | Large AI systems |
|--|--------|------------------|
| Energy per op | Very efficient biologically | Often wasteful at scale |
| Parallel search / memory recall | Limited | Strong |
| Grounded stakes / accountability | Native (body, law, reputation) | Designed, external |
| General flexible common sense in open world | Still strong in many niches | Uneven, improving |
| Long formal derivation at machine speed | Weak alone | Strong with tools |

Humans remain **special as locus of experience, legitimacy, and final responsibility** in ZEM terms — not as universal theorem-proving champions.

### 6. Residual
Human intelligence is **scaffoldable**: writing, science, institutions, and AI extend the effective envelope.  
Limits are real; **fixed ceiling on civilization-level intelligence** is not proven — only ceilings on **unaided individual brains**.

